 ## Delivery outline
 ```
 
 Requirements describe necessary behavior, not a preferred implementation unless the constraint is real. Use durable IDs such as `FR-101`; never renumber an existing PRD merely to make the document prettier.
+
+## WIGTN output contract
+
+For a feature with UI, the PRD must include these implementation artifacts. Keep
+them concise, but do not replace them with prose:
+
+- a User Roles table that states permissions and prohibited actions;
+- a Pages table with route, access role, and whether FE components exist;
+- a State Matrix covering Empty, Loading, Error, and Success for each relevant page;
+- a User Flow rendered as a Mermaid diagram;
+- functional requirements with stable IDs;
+- measurable, numeric NFR targets, or an explicitly owned open decision when a
+  target cannot yet be justified;
+- acceptance criteria in Given/When/Then form and mapped to requirement IDs;
+- server-side authorization rules for protected and destructive actions;
+- Non-Goals and implementation phases mapped to requirement IDs.
+
+These are project conventions, not suggestions. Include every applicable item
+even when the brief does not name it.
